{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Fear not, Abram, I am a shield to you.</b> It is possible to interpret that in this verse He promised him three things. <b>The first</b>: that He promised him [protection] from the fear of the kings whom he had slain, for one says 'fear not' only to one who is afraid — for he was afraid of the sons of the kings, lest they take vengeance against him for their fathers; therefore He said 'I am a shield to you,' that is, from the fear of the kings. <b>The second</b>: that He promised him the tidings of a son, and this is what He said, 'your reward shall be very great' (שכרך הרבה). Now it should have said שכרך רב, but He added the two hehs, for from the two of them Isaac was born — the heh in Sarah and the heh in Abraham; and this is the promise of this world (העוה\"ז). <b>The third</b>: the promise of the world to come (העוה\"ב), from what He added מאד ('exceedingly'), which alludes to the world to come, in the manner of what is written (Job 35:15), 'ולא ידע בפש מאד' — for Elihu seized Job for denying providence, and he would say to him that Job continually counts all day long his sufferings and pains, and did not know the great repose prepared for the righteous in the world to come. And since these three promises — one is explicit and two are by allusion — and Abraham followed what was revealed, and did not understand the allusion included in the words of the Holy One, blessed be He, therefore he needed to ask, 'What will You give me,' that is, what will my reward be, given that I have no children and I go childless — alone without children, from the language of (Jeremiah 17:6) 'כערער בערבה' — 'and one who goes out and comes in my house is none but Eliezer, a stranger, whom I acquired from Damascus, not from my father's house and not from my land.' And then the Holy One, blessed be He, explained to him the two that He had alluded to: the promise of this world is what He said, 'this one shall not be your heir, but rather he who shall come forth from your innards'; the promise of the world to come is from what He said, 'he shall be your heir' (הוא יירשך), for 'He' (הוא) is the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, whose inheritance you shall be, in the manner of (Exodus 34) 'ונחלתנו,' and this is clear." "<b>And the Ramban wrote</b> that what is said, 'and behold, the word of HaShem came to him, saying' — he had not yet finished [saying] <b>behold, the son of my house</b> when the word of HaShem came to him suddenly, <b>this one shall not be your heir</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:32.929059210Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}